
Subqueries are one of the most frequently tested SQL topics in interviews, including EY. A subquery is simply a query written inside another SQL query.

Syntax

SELECT column_name
FROM table_name
WHERE column_name OPERATOR (
    SELECT column_name
    FROM table_name
);
1. Students with marks greater than average ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Table: Students
id	name	marks
1	Ram	80
2	John	60
3	Sara	90
4	Priya	70
Query
SELECT *
FROM Students
WHERE marks > (
    SELECT AVG(marks)
    FROM Students
);
Output
name	marks
Ram	80
Sara	90
